	<span slot="title">About</span>
	<p slot="subtitle" class="subtitle">Semantic Signal is maintained by one developer, in the evenings.</p>

	<section class="section">
		<h2>Who</h2>
		<p>The author publishes as <strong>@qrak</strong>. The project is developed in the author's own time, alone. It is not a commercial product and has no funding.</p>
	</section>

	<section class="section">
		<h2>The project</h2>
		<p>An open-source LLM trading agent: it reads candlestick charts as images, keeps memory of closed trades, and applies deterministic risk limits before a decision is booked. Capital is simulated.</p>
		<p>The executor — the separate service that places orders — runs against an exchange testnet. That path stays on testnet until it has been verified, and the site says so.</p>
		<p>History: <a href="/story/">the full development history</a>. Numbers: <a href="/results/">the results page</a>.</p>
	</section>

	<section class="section">
		<h2>Repositories</h2>
		<ul>
			<li><a href="https://github.com/qrak/LLM_trader" target="_blank" rel="noopener">qrak/LLM_trader</a> — the main project: reasoning engine, Numba indicator library, vector memory, dashboard and this site.</li>
			<li><a href="https://github.com/qrak/ti_numba" target="_blank" rel="noopener">qrak/ti_numba</a> — the technical indicators, extracted as a standalone library.</li>
			<li><a href="https://github.com/qrak/DiscordCryptoAnalyzer" target="_blank" rel="noopener">qrak/DiscordCryptoAnalyzer</a> — the earlier bot, kept for the history.</li>
		</ul>
	</section>

	<section class="section">
		<h2>How the code is maintained</h2>
		<ul>
			<li><strong>2,728 collected tests</strong> (all of them run in CI), ruff and pyright in CI — <code>python -m pytest tests -q -m "not integration"</code>.</li>
			<li><strong>CHANGELOG.md</strong> records decisions, reversals and mistakes, including a brain-learning reset after a losing streak.</li>
			<li><strong>AGENTS.md</strong> per package documents the conventions and the verification gates for contributors and coding agents.</li>
		</ul>
	</section>

